{
  "dom_id": "step-q129499",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14163757/assets/3812ff158f2268f78bbc22cc0fa11f86fd8506a78ce05104df04fef1fe39d037.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?",
  "worked_solution": "We find the ranges of the individual pieces, and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (-4,-2)$ is $(-2,1)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [2,4)$ is $[2,4)$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $(-2,1)\\cup [2,4).$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the values $y=-2,$ $y=1$ and $y=4$ are NOT valid outputs of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use parentheses $(…)$ instead of brackets $[…]$ at these endpoints.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
